      "html": "<p>One of the most beautiful tetras of South America is available now in brilliantly colored wild-caught specimens. The Amapa tetra is an unrivalled eye-catcher for any well-suited community tank for South American fishes.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/hyphessobrycon-amapaensis/",
      "html": "<p>As usual, among these wild-caught fishes were also specimens of other species, so-called by-catches. This gives a good idea about the community of species the Amapa tetra lives in in the wild and also suggests perfect tankmates: Marbled hatchetfish, Carnegiella strigata; Dwarf pencilfish, Nannostomus marginatus; Head-and-taillight tetra, Hemigrammus ocellifer.</p>"
